DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     Function ddwwaarrff__ssrrccffiilleess() returns the source file names associated with a
     compilation unit.  Source file names are returned as an array of NUL-ter‐
     minated strings.

     Argument _d_i_e should reference a DWARF debugging information entry de‐
     scriptor with source file information, see dwarf(3).  Argument _f_i_l_e_n_a_m_e_s
     should point to a location that will hold a pointer to the returned array
     of file names.  Argument _f_i_l_e_n_a_m_e_c_o_u_n_t should point to a location that
     will hold the number of file names returned.  If argument _e_r_r is not
     NULL, it will be used to store error information in case of an error.

   MMeemmoorryy MMaannaaggeemmeenntt
     The memory areas used for the file names and for array of pointers being
     returned are managed by the DWARF(3) library.  The application should not
     attempt to directly free these memory areas.  Portable code should indi‐
     cate that the memory areas are to be freed by using dwarf_dealloc(3).

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     Function ddwwaarrff__ssrrccffiilleess() returns DW_DLV_OK when it succeeds.  In case of
     an error, it returns DW_DLV_ERROR and sets the argument _e_r_r.

EERRRROORRSS
     Function ddwwaarrff__ssrrccffiilleess() can fail with:

     [DW_DLE_ARGUMENT]  One of the arguments _d_i_e, _f_i_l_e_n_a_m_e_s or _f_i_l_e_n_a_m_e_c_o_u_n_t
